  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection of Nyekweri Forest by local communities, Trans Mara Subcounty, Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nyekweri Forest is located to the west of the Maasai Mara Nature Reserve and remains an important refuge for threatened wildlife. The project assisted the approximately 1,000 Maasai living in the area in developing a biocultural protocol based on their traditions and cultural values. Working together with the local project partner, the project improved exchanges with the administration at regional level in order to achieve legal recognition as a conservancy. The project also strengthened income-generating activities to reduce deforestation for charcoal production. These included for example eco-tourism, improved animal husbandry and honey production. These project measures contributed to preventing forest loss beyond the lifetime of the project. Women were trained to improve the production and sale of traditional bead jewelry and to manage this income independently. Particular emphasis was placed on women&#x2019;s independent income and on strengthening their role in traditional community bodies.</narrative>
  </description>
